{"version":3,"term":{"cols":100,"rows":32},"timestamp":1793508661,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"command":"bash /home/claude/solves/narnia/L2.sh","title":"Narnia L2 -> narnia3: buf[128] strcpy overflow; shellcode written in vim, assembled with nasm, swept return address","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/bash"}}
[0.002, "o", "$ ssh narnia2@narnia.labs.overthewire.org -p 2226   # password 0h8Tj5fxbv\r\n$ cat /narnia/narnia2.c   # char buf[128]; strcpy(buf, argv[1]);\r\n$ objdump: sub $0x80,%esp; strcpy@plt -> buffer at ebp-0x80, ret at offset 132\r\n$ readelf: GNU_STACK RWE -> the stack is executable; ASLR is off\r\n$ gdb: break before strcpy, print $ebp-0x80 and $ebp+4\r\n$ vim /tmp/l2.asm -> write the shellcode (marker, setreuid, execve)\r\n$ nasm -f elf32, objdump the object, objcopy -O binary, xxd the bytes\r\n$ vim /tmp/e_narnia2.py -> write the exploit: NOP sled + shellcode + saved ebp\r\n$   + return address, sweeping 0xffffd000..0xffffe800 for the PWN! marker\r\n$ python3 /tmp/e_narnia2.py -> shell as narnia3\r\n"]
